+# Workspace notes for AI coding agents — Super Market (Monorepo)
+
+## Big picture 🔧
+- Monorepo with two main apps:
+  - **Backend**: Java Spring Boot app in `SuperMarket Backend/` (Maven, JPA, JWT auth).
+  - **Frontend**: React + Vite app in `SuperMarket New Frontend/` (Tailwind, Vite, Playwright E2E).
+- Dev uses H2 (local profile) and MySQL for production; Docker Compose orchestrates frontend/backend/mysql (see `DOCKER_DEPLOYMENT.md`).
+
+## Quick dev commands ✅
+- Frontend (Windows paths may include spaces):
+  - cd "SuperMarket New Frontend" && npm install && npm run dev
+- Backend (local profile):
+  - cd "SuperMarket Backend" && ./mvnw.cmd -DskipTests package
+  - java -jar target/SuperMarketBackend-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar --spring.profiles.active=local
+- Start both (helper): `start-dev.ps1` (starts frontend + backend and opens admin login).
+- Docker (prod-like): follow `DOCKER_DEPLOYMENT.md` or run `docker-compose up -d --build` from repo root.
+
+## Important environment / wiring ⚙️
+- API base: code reads `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL` (frontend `src/utils/api.js`) and defaults to `http://localhost:8080/api`.
+- Docs and `.env.example` reference `VITE_API_BASE_URL` (docker); **be aware of this mismatch**—set `VITE_API_URL` (or both) to point at `http://localhost:8080`.
+- `.env.example`, `docker-compose.yml` and `DOCKER_DEPLOYMENT.md` contain canonical deployment environment variables.
+
+## Auth & security patterns 🔐
+- JWT-based, stateless security (see `JwtSecurityConfig.java`).
+  - Public: `/api/admin/login`, `/api/dev/**`, some `/api/audit/*` endpoints.
+  - Admin protected: `/api/admin/**`, `/api/audit/**` require roles `ADMIN` or `SUPER_ADMIN`.
+- Frontend stores token as `adminToken` in `localStorage` and admin profile as `admin`.
+- Local dev seeds default admin via `LocalDataLoader` → `admin@supermart.com` / `admin123`.
+
+## Testing & E2E 🧪
+- Playwright E2E target: `npm run test:e2e` (ensure `npx playwright install` first).
+- E2E tests use a dev-only endpoint `/api/dev/create-user` to create test data (see `e2e/admin.spec.js`). Keep dev endpoints stable if tests depend on them.
+
+## Code & architectural conventions 📚
+- Backend layering: `controller` → `service` → `repository` + `entities` (JPA). Package root is `in.main`.
+- Controllers use `@RequestMapping("/api/...")`. Add new APIs under `/api` and only expose them as needed in `JwtSecurityConfig`.
+- CORS and static file serving: `WebConfig` exposes `/uploads/**` and allows local origins (3000/3001).
+- Error handling is centralized using `GlobalExceptionHandler` (look for `@ControllerAdvice`).
+
+## Files to consult first (high signal) 📄
+- `DOCKER_DEPLOYMENT.md` — deployment + Docker Compose architecture (ports, envs).
+- `README_DEV.md` — local dev scripts & quick start.
+- `SuperMarket Backend/src/main/resources/application-local.properties` — local DB/profile config (H2).
+- `LocalDataLoader.java` — seeds (default admin credentials).
+- `SuperMarket New Frontend/src/utils/api.js` — how frontend builds API base and attaches JWT.
+- `JwtSecurityConfig.java`, `WebConfig.java` — security/CORS expectations.
+- `.env.example`, `docker-compose.yml` — production env variables and overrides.
+
+## Quick PR guidance / patterns ✅
+- When adding an admin-only endpoint: create controller mapping under `/api/admin/...`, add business logic in `service`, add DB access in `repository`, and update `JwtSecurityConfig` if needed.
+- For front-end API calls, rely on `api.js` axios instance (it injects Authorization header from `adminToken`).
+- Add E2E tests only if they can run against dev-seeded data or the test creates its own data via `/api/dev/**`.
+
+## Known quirks & gotchas ⚠️
+- Path names contain spaces (e.g., "SuperMarket New Frontend") — wrap paths in quotes on CLI on Windows.
+- Env var name mismatch: `VITE_API_URL` (code) vs `VITE_API_BASE_URL` (docs/docker). Prefer setting both to be safe.
+- Credentials and some DB passwords appear in checked-in properties for convenience — avoid using them for production and use `.env`/secrets instead.
+
+---
+## One-page quick-start (copy-paste) 🚀
+Prereqs: Java 17+, Maven, Node 18+, Docker (optional).
+
+1. Frontend (dev):
+   cd "SuperMarket New Frontend" && npm install && npm run dev
+2. Backend (local profile):
+   cd "SuperMarket Backend" && ./mvnw.cmd -DskipTests package && java -jar target/SuperMarketBackend-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.jar --spring.profiles.active=local
+3. Start both (helper): `start-dev.ps1`
+4. E2E (Playwright): cd "SuperMarket New Frontend" && npx playwright install && npm run test:e2e
+5. Docker (prod-like): from repo root `cp .env.example .env` and `docker-compose up -d --build`
+
+## Checklist — Adding a new API / endpoint 🧭
+- Add controller under `SuperMarket Backend/src/main/java/in/main/controller/` with `@RequestMapping("/api/your")` and HTTP methods.
+- Implement business logic in a new or existing `service/` class.
+- Add DB access in `repository/` (extend `JpaRepository`) and update `entities/` if schema changes are required.
+- Add DTOs and mappers if the payload differs from entities.
+- Protect the endpoint via roles in `JwtSecurityConfig` (if admin-only use `/api/admin/**`).
+- Add unit tests (service) and integration/E2E tests for cross-stack flows. Use `/api/dev/**` helpers for test data when available.
+- Update `DOCKER_DEPLOYMENT.md` and `.env.example` if new services or env vars are required.
+
